\import{dt-macros}
\import{ltp-macros}
\title{Decision properties}
\taxon{Definition}
%\author{liamoc}
\meta{source}{(from [[amjad-vanglabbeek-oconnor-2026]])}
\p{A \em{decision} property (called \em{strong monitorable} by [Amjad et al.](amjad-vanglabbeek-oconnor-2026)) is a [property](ltp-0003) for which \em{both} confirmation and refutation only require a finite prefix. In other words, decision properties are the intersection of a [safety](ltp-0004) and [guarantee](ltp-0005) property. 
This makes decision properties the clopen sets in our [topology](ltp-0007). A simple characterisation from topology is that #{P} is a decision property iff #{\sc{P}=\gk{P}}.}